  "critical": false,
  "description": "Emerging and next-generation radioisotope power conversion technologies beyond heritage thermoelectric and Stirling systems. Covers thermophotovoltaic (TPV) cells that convert emitter infrared radiation at 30%+ efficiency, betavoltaic nuclear batteries delivering microwatt-scale power for decades from Ni-63 and tritium, alpha-voltaic cells using wide-bandgap GaN and SiC junctions, and advanced segmented thermoelectric materials. These approaches push specific power, lifetime, and miniaturisation beyond conventional RTG limits but remain at TRL 3-4 except for commercial betavoltaics.",
